1. What is strategy pattern ?
- Strategy pattern is a behavioral design pattern.
- Lets you define family of algorithms, which can be inter changeable at run time
- Strategy Pattern = Choose behavior at runtime without changing the code that uses it

2. In google maps you can choose car route, Walking route or cycling route
- Same app -> Different strategies (Algorithms)
- Without strategy pattern we might need to use if-else, this causes the code to be too complex,
hard to extend this code this violates the open/close principle.

if (type == "car") { ... }
else if (type == "walk") { ... }
else if (type == "bike") { ... }

3. Structure of Strategy Pattern
- Strategy Interface (interface/abstract)
- Concrete Strategies (Different Implementation)
- Context (Decide which strategy to use)

4. Key Benefits
- Removes if-else
- Easy to add new strategies
- Follows open/ close principle
- Cleaner and testable

5. When to use strategy pattern
- When you have multiple ways to do the same way
- You want to switch logic at runtime
- You want to avoid huge conditional logic


